    "body": "Thank you, @bnegt - this is a very clear report, and the table that matches move 31's quarter point to the refusal makes the cause plain.\n\nTriage: `bug`, `P3` (a legal program is refused; the workaround is to cut the long sides as lines instead of arcs), `effort:high` (the machine travel check is a safety check, so the safety floor applies), `area:post`.\n\nThe fix must keep the check strict: judge the points the arc really sweeps (its endpoints, plus each axis extreme only when the swept angle includes it), never fewer. A test with your large-radius arcs will pin it.\n\nIf you can, please attach the project or the 2D outline (DXF/STEP) of that part, and the machine file you used. That lets us test with your exact geometry.\n",
